# =============================================================================
# Store — DELETE (close) requests (VS Code REST Client) — DELETE /api/v1/stores/{id} (ADMIN)
# =============================================================================
# Semantics (ticket 0010 — closed stores are HONEST-DEAD):
#   - DELETE closes a store (status → CLOSED): 204. The row survives at the
#     DB level (audit: last_store_admin_id is filled), but it is INVISIBLE to
#     the API — no reads, no updates, no re-close.
#   - After close: GET → 404, DELETE again → 404, PUT → 404. Dead is dead.
#   - Closing releases the store admin's seat: one NON-CLOSED store per
#     admin, so a closed store's admin can immediately take a new store.
#
# How to run:
#   1. Start the backend: `docker compose up -d --build` — http://localhost:4000
#   2. Click the "Send Request" CodeLens above any request, IN ORDER, in one
#      sitting (captures are session-scoped).
#
# Prerequisites (admin persona):
#   Signup admin@devtunde.com with Password123! once, then promote in MySQL:
#     update users set role = 'ROLE_ADMIN' where email = 'admin@devtunde.com';
#
# Notes:
#   - All data is FAKE (devtunde.com emails, Nigerian numbers).
#   - The automated suite for these endpoints: StoreApiTests (src/test/java).
#   - Re-runnable: the manager persona, brand and contact email are minted
#     fresh each run with {{$timestamp}} — no 409 collisions with prior runs.
#   - Access tokens expire after 15 MINUTES. If tokened requests suddenly 401,
#     re-send the SETUP requests from the top (they mint and re-capture).
#   - REST Client captures die on file/VS Code reopen. If you see raw {{...}}
#     template text being sent or sudden 500s, re-send the setup requests
#     from the top — never continue on a dead capture.
#   - Expected codes: 204 close, 404 dead/unknown store, 401 no/invalid
#     token, 403 non-admin, 405 wrong method, 201 seat-release proof.
# =============================================================================

@storeUrl = http://localhost:4000/api/v1/stores
@authUrl = http://localhost:4000/api/v1/auth

### 1 — Setup: login the admin persona
# Expected: 200
# @name adminLogin
POST {{authUrl}}/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "admin@devtunde.com",
  "password": "Password123!"
}

### 2 — Setup: signup the store manager (minted fresh each run)
# Expected: 201 — never 409, the timestamp makes the persona unique
# @name sellerSignup
POST {{authUrl}}/signup
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fullName": "Doomed Manager",
  "email": "probe-close-mgr-{{$timestamp}}@devtunde.com",
  "password": "Password123!",
  "phone": "+2348031234580"
}

### 3 — Setup: login the manager
# Expected: 200
# @name sellerLogin
POST {{authUrl}}/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{sellerSignup.response.body.user.email}}",
  "password": "Password123!"
}

### 4 — Setup: create the doomed store (minted brand)
# Expected: 201 — status ACTIVE
# @name storeOk
POST {{storeUrl}}
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{adminLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

{
  "brand": "Doomed Store {{$timestamp}}",
  "description": "Born to be closed",
  "storeType": "BRANCH",
  "storeAdminPublicId": "{{sellerLogin.response.body.user.publicId}}",
  "contact": {
    "address": "12 Market Road, Lagos",
    "phone": "08012345678",
    "email": "doomed-{{$timestamp}}@devtunde.com"
  }
}

### 5 — Close the store
# Expected: 204 — status flips to CLOSED; the row survives invisibly at the
# DB level (last_store_admin_id keeps the audit copy)
DELETE {{storeUrl}}/{{storeOk.response.body.publicId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

### 6 — Fetch the closed store
# Expected: 404 — closed = honest-dead for EVERYONE, including the admin
GET {{storeUrl}}/{{storeOk.response.body.publicId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

### 7 — Close it again
# Expected: 404 — no idempotent second delete; the corpse is already gone
DELETE {{storeUrl}}/{{storeOk.response.body.publicId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

### 8 — Try to revive it via update
# Expected: 404 — PUT on a dead store 404s regardless of payload (Q4: dead
# stores are immutable; revival would need its own explicit endpoint someday)
PUT {{storeUrl}}/{{storeOk.response.body.publicId}}
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{adminLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

{
  "description": "Please come back"
}

### 9 — Close with no Authorization header
# Expected: 401 — the security filter runs before routing
DELETE {{storeUrl}}/{{storeOk.response.body.publicId}}

### 10 — Close with a garbage token
# Expected: 401
DELETE {{storeUrl}}/{{storeOk.response.body.publicId}}
Authorization: Bearer not-a-real-jwt

### 11 — Setup: signup the regular persona (fixed — she never holds a seat)
# Expected: 201 (409 if she already exists — either way the account exists)
# @name regularSignup
POST {{authUrl}}/signup
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fullName": "Bola Storeless",
  "email": "bola.storeless@devtunde.com",
  "password": "Password123!",
  "phone": "+2348031234571"
}

### 12 — Setup: login the regular persona
# Expected: 200
# @name regularLogin
POST {{authUrl}}/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "bola.storeless@devtunde.com",
  "password": "Password123!"
}

### 13 — Close as a regular user
# Expected: 403 — @PreAuthorize ADMIN fires BEFORE the service, so even a
# dead store's id answers 403 to a non-admin: permission precedes existence
DELETE {{storeUrl}}/{{storeOk.response.body.publicId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{regularLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

### 14 — Close a store id that never existed
# Expected: 404
DELETE {{storeUrl}}/99999999-9999-9999-9999-999999999999
Authorization: Bearer {{adminLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

### 15 — Wrong method against a single store
# Expected: 405 — no POST route exists on /stores/{id}
POST {{storeUrl}}/{{storeOk.response.body.publicId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

### 16 — Seat release (Q5): the closed store's admin takes a NEW store
# Expected: 201 — closing freed his seat (rule: one NON-CLOSED store per
# admin; his only store is CLOSED, so the seat is open again)
# @name storeReborn
POST {{storeUrl}}
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{adminLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

{
  "brand": "Reassigned Store {{$timestamp}}",
  "storeType": "KIOSK",
  "storeAdminPublicId": "{{sellerLogin.response.body.user.publicId}}",
  "contact": {
    "address": "45 New Address, Ikeja",
    "phone": "08087654321",
    "email": "reassigned-{{$timestamp}}@devtunde.com"
  }
}
